# Children and Adolescents; A Biocultural Approach to Psychological Development.

**Authors:** Alexander, Theron

## Abstract
In a discussion of psychological development separate sections are devoted to (1) biological and cultural influences on development, (2) development in infancy, early childhood, middle childhood, and adolescence, (3) physiological foundations of behavior, (4) motivation and cognitive development, (5) intellectual development, (6) imagination and creativity, (7) socialization, (8) social learning and authority, (9) developmental disorders, and (10) methods and theories contributing to child and adolescent psychology. Relevant research is reviewed. (EM)

